# Copy to .env — docker compose reads it — and choose how `find` turns a
# description ("the search box in the header") into an element on the page.
#
# Literal matching: no model, no key, no cost. `find` matches the page's own
# words (role + name); a query they do not contain returns no match, and says so.
BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_URL=""
BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_KEY=""
BROWSER_FIND_MODEL=""

# …or a model tier: any endpoint that speaks the Anthropic Messages API. Replace
# the three lines above with ONE of these blocks.
#
# OpenRouter — one key for hundreds of models, some of them free
# (key: https://openrouter.ai/keys, models: https://openrouter.ai/models):
# BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_KEY=<your OpenRouter key>
# BROWSER_FIND_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
#
# Anthropic:
# BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# BROWSER_FIND_INFERENCE_KEY=<your Anthropic key>
# BROWSER_FIND_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
